// The twin of fp_out_no_semantic_f.cg, with `: COLOR` written out
// (t_a15ec129).  The two must compile to the same PROGRAM - identical
// ucode - because an omitted output semantic on a fragment entry is not
// missing information: the reference binds it to COLOR0 without being
// told.  The CONTAINERS differ by one string, the declared semantic, which
// the reference records as UNDEFINED when it was omitted; ours matches
// each of the reference's two containers byte for byte.
void main(float4 color : TEXCOORD0,
          out float4 oColor : COLOR)
{
    oColor = color;
}
